#hasheq((content-digest . "d69c980d65eba8948dfc015afaaeb2b177ca9a3d0507be84fd1142208ed76db9") (milestone . 896) (plan-id . "fb67e0429ed155a4b4e3f31afe3ef3ca7748ee891c06247b11e5e2a86cfebd75") (report . "Fourteen independent review rounds (R1-R14) against the frozen W5 wave doc. R1 found three defects (nested provenance fields disabled by non-matching ancestor keys; the F13 restore could not restore a stale PLAN.md; a legacy manifest hash broken by a trailing empty element) - all remediated with regression tests. R2 refused a non-reproducible matrix recorded head and the generator now reads the pinned observation from the committed matrix (regeneration is byte-identical). R3 refused an unbound tree/digest gap (tree/head pairing implemented) and R4 refused a non-canonical current-wave SHA256SUMS (canonical regeneration gate plus red fixture). R5 refused timing values from unrelated numeric fields and an uncaught exception on malformed SUMS lines (both fixed with tests). R6 and R7 refused non-recursive JSON coverage (all five checks now traverse nested subdirectories, raw/ exempt). R8 refused the missing F7 register guard, unverified recorded sha256 fields, and the intra-JSON-only cross-artifact check (F7 guard registered; recorded-digest-to-file verification and bound-report agreement added). R9 refused tree fields walked as commits, a subtractive timing set, and non-Python-compatible canonical escapes (all fixed with tests). R10 refused an order-dependent report scan and one-level artifact discovery. R11 refused branch-dependent gate strictness and a crash on directory-relative current-wave SUMS entries. R12 refused discovery that did not implement the documented artifacts/**/v*/ scope. R13 required the F7 contract's exact head binding for head-claiming fields (implementation-sha/reviewed-sha/verified-head/receipt-head must equal the tip) while pinned observation heads keep ancestor semantics because a committed artifact cannot contain its own commit hash. R14 reviewed the final delta and found no blocking defect. Every accepted item is documented in docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md; the lint reports 941 historical provenance notes and zero drift at this head.") (reviewed-sha . "c60adbd24e13d373f01ea35ab5b15547a61d7c03") (reviewer . "pi-reviewer-subagent:readonly-w5-impl-review-r14:campaign-v1.00.31-w5-4a19d60b4:2026-09-23") (schema-version . 2) (scope . "W5 artifact provenance and determinism: scripts/ci/verify-artifact-provenance.rkt (SHA256SUMS binding incl. recursive coverage and both historical spellings, provenance heads with exact binding for head-claiming fields and ancestor semantics for pinned observation heads, paired tree validation, canonical JSON with Python-compatible escapes, cross-artifact prose/structured timing agreement including bound markdown reports, and recorded-digest-to-file verification), recursive artifact discovery over artifacts/**/v*, the F7 register guard in tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt, the coordinator artifact-provenance gate with branch-independent current-wave derivation, tests/test-artifact-provenance.rkt (22 tests), the deterministic generator and artifacts under artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w5/, docs/reports/ARTIFACT-PROVENANCE-v1.00.31.md, and the F13 frozen-contract staleness guard in extensions/gsd/{plan-snapshot,campaign-state,campaign-repository}.rkt at implementation head c60adbd24e13d373f01ea35ab5b15547a61d7c03 with content digest d69c980d65eba8948dfc015afaaeb2b177ca9a3d0507be84fd1142208ed76db9.") (timestamp . "2026-09-23T00:00:00Z") (verdict . "APPROVED") (wave . "W5"))
